{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fe2f177f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Building Defect AI — Notebook workflow\n",
    "\n",
    "Run from the repository root. Expected data layout: `dataset/BD3_split/{train,val,test}/<class_name>/...`.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Task:** classify images into the seven BD3 labels. This notebook records the method, why it is used, the result and its interpretation. Do not treat model predictions as professional inspection findings."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "58060e5c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "from torchvision import datasets, models\n",
    "ROOT = Path.cwd()\n",
    "DATA = ROOT / \"dataset\" / \"BD3_split\"\n",
    "DEVICE = torch.device(\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")\n",
    "print(\"Project:\", ROOT)\n",
    "print(\"Device:\", DEVICE)\n",
    "assert DATA.exists(), f\"Dataset folder not found: {DATA}. Run from the project root and add the dataset.\"\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2bb68d59",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Load dataset metadata\n",
    "\n",
    "`ImageFolder` infers labels from subfolder names. This keeps labels consistent with the directory structure. We inspect counts before training because class imbalance can affect metrics."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "c9136a38",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from collections import Counter\n",
    "from torchvision.datasets import ImageFolder\n",
    "splits = {}\n",
    "for split in [\"train\", \"val\", \"test\"]:\n",
    "    ds = ImageFolder(DATA / split)\n",
    "    splits[split] = ds\n",
    "    print(f\"\\\\n{split}: {len(ds)} images\")\n",
    "    print(dict(Counter(ds.targets)))\n",
    "print(\"Class order:\", splits[\"train\"].classes)\n",
    "for split, ds in splits.items():\n",
    "    assert ds.classes == splits[\"train\"].classes, f\"Class order mismatch in {split}\"\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "755a79d9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Visualise class distribution\n",
    "\n",
    "A bar chart reveals whether some classes are represented much more often than others. It does not by itself prove the model will be biased, but it helps interpret per-class recall."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "bb70299c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "counts = {s: [splits[s].targets.count(i) for i in range(len(splits[s].classes))] for s in splits}\n",
    "x = range(len(splits[\"train\"].classes))\n",
    "for s, vals in counts.items():\n",
    "    plt.plot(list(x), vals, marker=\"o\", label=s)\n",
    "plt.xticks(list(x), splits[\"train\"].classes, rotation=35, ha=\"right\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Number of images\"); plt.title(\"Images per class and split\"); plt.legend(); plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "523f12a9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "Write down any imbalance, unusual image conditions, and whether train/validation/test class counts look plausible. The recorded split sizes for this project are 2,378 / 792 / 795. A duplicate or near-duplicate audit is still required before claiming fully independent generalisation."
   ]
  }
 ],
